  "dst": "same canvas with the least-populated non-axis color mask completed across the axis",
  "transform": "mirror every pixel of the unique least-populated non-axis color across the row, column, main-diagonal, or anti-diagonal axis; leave all original pixels unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: square, 9-17 rows/cols (odd for row/col axis; even or odd for diagonal axis)
  background: single dominant color filling most of the grid
  axis:
    type: one of row, col, main_diag, anti_diag (all four attested)
    color: one foreground color spans the full row/col/diagonal
    position: row/col axis at exact center index; diagonals span corner to corner
  foreground_colors:
    count: exactly 2 non-axis foreground colors
    placement: ALL foreground pixels (both colors) on the SAME side of the axis; opposite side is entirely background
    mirror_color: the color with strictly smaller total pixel count (uniquely minimum)
    non_mirror_color: the other color with larger area
  mirror_color:
    total_area: 4-12 pixels
    components: 1-3 connected components, each 2-7 pixels
    constraint: reflected positions must land on background cells only (no overlap with non-mirror objects)
  non_mirror_color:
    total_area: 5-17 pixels
    components: 1-3 connected components, each 3-9 pixels
  area_ratio: mirror_area / non_mirror_area in 0.5-0.8 (strictly less than 1)
  output: input preserved; mirror_color pixels reflected across axis onto background cells

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N (9-17, odd if row/col axis chosen; square always).
    2. Choose axis type (row/col/main_diag/anti_diag) and axis color.
    3. Draw the axis on an N x N background grid.
    4. Choose one side of the axis for all foreground placement.
    5. Pick mirror_color and non_mirror_color (distinct from bg and axis).
    6. Place non_mirror objects (1-3 components, total 5-17 px) on the chosen side, avoiding the axis.
    7. Place mirror objects (1-3 components, total 4-12 px, strictly less than non_mirror area) on the chosen side, avoiding axis and non_mirror pixels.
    8. Verify all mirror pixels reflect onto background cells (not onto non_mirror or axis); reject/retry component if not.
    9. Input = the grid so far. Output = input + reflected mirror pixels painted with mirror_color.
```
